      "content": "Ethiopia Delivers Over 1 Million Digital Business Registration, Licensing Services - allAfrica.com AllAfrica English (current) En Français Toggle navigation My Account Toggle navigation AllAfrica My Account English (current) En Français Ethiopia Delivers Over 1 Million Digital Business Registration, Licensing Services 26 October 2026 Ethiopian News Agency (Addis Ababa) Addis Ababa — Ethiopia provided more than 1.08 million business registration and licensing services digitally over a three-month period, according to the Ministry of Trade and Regional Integration. The milestone highlights ongoing national efforts to streamline business procedures and expand online public services. The ministry's latest online services report reveals that 1,088,787 services were delivered across federal institutions, regional states, and city administrations, underscoring the expanding role of digital platforms in the country's commercial administration. Among the regions, Oromia Regional State recorded the highest volume with 441,550 services provided. Addis Ababa followed with 204,512, Amhara with 156,193, and South Ethiopia with 101,891. By service category, trade name clearance accounted for the largest share, with 579,785 services delivered. Business license renewals followed with 122,730, while license amendments totaled 107,317. New business registrations accounted for 60,409 services. The ministry said the digital system was helping reduce bureaucratic burdens on the business community while improving the efficiency, accessibility and transparency of public service delivery. The expansion of digital business registration and licensing services is part of Ethiopia's broader digital transformation agenda, which aims to modernize public administration, simplify procedures and improve access to government services through technology. Read the original article on ENA . Tagged: Ethiopia East Africa Business ICT Copyright © 2026 Ethiopian News Agency . All rights reserved. Distributed by AllAfrica Global Media ( allAfrica.com ). To contact the copyright holder directly for corrections — or for permission to republish or make other authorized use of this material, click here. AllAfrica publishes around 600 reports a day from more than 90 news organizations and over 500 other institutions and individuals , representing a diversity of positions on every topic. We publish news and views ranging from vigorous opponents of governments to government publications and spokespersons. Publishers named above each report are responsible for their own content, which AllAfrica does not have the legal right to edit or correct. Articles and commentaries that identify allAfrica.com as the publisher are produced or commissioned by AllAfrica . To address comments or complaints, please Contact us . AllAfrica is a voice of, by and about Africa - aggregating, producing and distributing 600 news and information items daily from over 90 African news organizations and our own reporters to an African and global public. We operate from Cape Town, Dakar, Abuja, Johannesburg, Nairobi and Washington DC. Support our work Sign up for our newsletter For Advertisers Subscribe © 2026 AllAfrica Privacy Policy Contact Us About Us AllAfrica - All the Time Close Sign up for free AllAfrica Newsletters Get the latest in African news delivered straight to your inbox Submit By submitting above, you agree to our privacy policy . Success! Almost finished... We need to confirm your email address. To complete the process, please follow the instructions in the email we just sent you. Error! Error! There was a problem processing your submission. Please try again later.",
      "summary": "Ethiopia has successfully delivered over 1.08 million digital business registration and licensing services within a three-month period, as reported by the Ministry of Trade and Regional Integration. This achievement reflects the country's commitment to enhancing business procedures and expanding online public services. The report indicates that 1,088,787 services were provided across various federal institutions, regional states, and city administrations, with Oromia Regional State leading at 441,550 services. Addis Ababa and Amhara followed with 204,512 and 156,193 services, respectively. The most common service was trade name clearance, accounting for 579,785 services, while business license renewals and amendments also contributed significantly. The digital system aims to alleviate bureaucratic challenges for businesses, improving efficiency, accessibility, and transparency in public service delivery. This initiative is part of Ethiopia's broader digital transformation agenda, which seeks to modernize public administration and enhance access to government services through technology.",
